==Serbo-Croatian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|sh|uza}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{recons|vъz|lang=sla-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/uz/|lang=sh}}

===Preposition===
{{sh-preposition|r|уз}}{{attention|sh|tone?}}

# (''with accusative'') [[up]], [[upward]]
#: ''ići uz stepenice'' — to go upstairs
#: ''uz brdo'' — uphill
#: ''iz r(ij)eku'' — upriver
#: ''peti/penjati se uz konopac'' — to climb a rope
# (''with accusative'') [[next]] to, [[beside]], [[by]]
#: ''uz cestu'' — next to the road
#: ''uza samu granicu'' — on the very border
# (''with accusative'') [[with]], [[along]] with (circumstances or conditions accompanying the action)
#: ''uz sm(ij)eh/plač'' — wile laughing/crying
#: ''uz p(j)esmu'' — while singing
#: ''uz piće'' — while drinking, while having a drink
#: ''p(j)evati uz klavir'' — to sing while the piano is playing
# (''with accusative'') [[in spite of]], [[despite]] (={{term|pored|pȍred|lang=sh}})
#: ''uza sve to'' — despite all that

====Usage notes====
The variant form {{term|uza|lang=sh}} is used before enclitics and consonants which would make it difficult to pronounce.

